{"id":28833,"slug":"a-matter-of-life-and-death","title":"A Matter of Life and Death","year":1946,"country":"United Kingdom","duration":104,"spine":939,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/28833-a-matter-of-life-and-death","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/69bacb52c7796d3fc2e37c7e1e2ddd6b/NGlO5lUTrsZN3usOFgwxTBaFHTOtGq_large.jpg","description":"After miraculously surviving a jump from his burning plane, RAF pilot Peter Carter (David Niven) encounters the American radio operator (Kim Hunter) to whom he has just delivered his dying wishes, and, face-to-face on a tranquil English beach, the pair fall in love. When a messenger from the hereafter arrives to correct the bureaucratic error that spared his life, Peter must mount a fierce defense for his right to stay on earth—painted by production designer Alfred Junge and cinematographer Jack Cardiff as a rich Technicolor Eden—climbing a wide staircase to stand trial in a starkly beautiful, black-and-white modernist afterlife. Intended to smooth tensions between the wartime allies Britain and America, Michael Powell and Emeric Pressburger’s richly humanistic A Matter of Life and Death traverses time and space to make a case for the transcendent value of love.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Michael Powell","slug":"michael-powell"},{"name":"Emeric Pressburger","slug":"emeric-pressburger"}],"cast":[{"actor":"David Niven","role":"Peter Carter","slug":"david-niven"},{"actor":"Roger Livesey","role":"Dr. Reeves","slug":"roger-livesey"},{"actor":"Raymond Massey","role":"Abraham Farlan","slug":"raymond-massey"},{"actor":"Kim Hunter","role":"June","slug":"kim-hunter"},{"actor":"Marius Goring","role":"Conductor 71","slug":"marius-goring"},{"actor":"Abraham Sofaer","role":"The judge","slug":"abraham-sofaer"},{"actor":"Robert Coote","role":"Bob","slug":"robert-coote"},{"actor":"Joan Maude","role":"Chief recorder","slug":"joan-maude"},{"actor":"Kathleen Byron","role":"An angel","slug":"kathleen